<title>CANADA: TABLE-Canada government cash balances fall in week.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Canada government cash balances fall in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances  fell in the week that ended July 30, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>				    Wk to July 30  Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  28.58   +0.483    +1.151</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     3.43   -1.514    -1.306</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	457.20   -0.020    -6.591</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 122.40    0.000   -31.800</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  32.15   -0.018    +1.907</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>					   June 97     May 97    June 96</p>
<p>M1					  72.65	71.01	62.82</p>
<p>M2					 393.61     391.81     392.49</p>
<p>M3					 507.14     505.67     482.38</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			June	  May</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-16.72	-14.59</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     726.76	714.36</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    105.65	102.60</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
